  ('144747885378904638', 'Gun Crazy', 1950, 'Crime, Romance, Drama', 'Joseph H. Lewis, Russell Harlan, Frank Heath', 'Dalton Trumbo, Millard Kaufman, MacKinlay Kantor', 'Peggy Cummins, John Dall, Berry Kroeger, Morris Carnovsky, Anabel Shaw, Harry Lewis, Nedrick Young, Trevor Bardette', null, 'Bart Tare is an ex-Army man who has a lifelong fixation with guns, he meets a kindred spirit in sharpshooter Annie Starr and goes to work at a carnival. After upsetting the carnival owner who lusts after Starr, they both get fired. Soon, on Starr''s behest, they embark on a crime spree for cash.', 'Bart Tare is an ex-Army man who has a lifelong fixation with guns, he meets a kindred spirit in sharpshooter Annie Starr and goes to work at a carnival. After upsetting the carnival owner who lusts after Starr, they both get fired. Soon, on Starr''s behest, they embark on a crime spree for cash.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/kC1IIitCJTZLwZyuQnKw4zaOaXc.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:18671'),
  ('572858788879687984', 'Gun for a Coward', 1956, 'Western', 'Abner Biberman, William Holland, George Robinson', 'R. Wright Campbell', 'Fred MacMurray, Jeffrey Hunter, Janice Rule, Chill Wills, Dean Stockwell, Josephine Hutchinson, Betty Lynn, Iron Eyes Cody', 'NR', 'A young cowboy, whose dedication to the principles of peace and reason has earned him a reputation for cowardice, overcomes his psychological aversion to violence after his elder brother unjustly censures him for not joining in a foolhardy gunfight in which their youngest brother is killed.', 'A young cowboy, whose dedication to the principles of peace and reason has earned him a reputation for cowardice, overcomes his psychological aversion to violence after his elder brother unjustly censures him for not joining in a foolhardy gunfight in which their youngest brother is killed.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/8woG8jAEpHev7jRXzAybl7Kzmwd.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:79103'),
